message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Autonomous Driving: A Multi-Module Algorithmic Framework"
abstract: >-
  An autonomous driving system comprising four algorithmically coupled
  modules: Perception, PathPlanning, Control, and SLAM. The system is
  designed for an Ackermann-steered vehicle operating in indoor structured
  environments under embedded-platform real-time constraints. The framework
  achieves 0.096 m SLAM position RMSE, sub-5 cm perception tracking RMSE,
  and 0.037 m lateral control RMSE on representative test scenarios.
